---
import Project from '../../layouts/Project.astro';
const stages = [['JSON decode',4.88,6.71,7.21],['Parse to OrderBookData',9.96,13.54,17.76],['Build payload',14.13,18.72,25.30],['Serialise payload',2.83,3.83,4.17],['ZMQ socket.send',.17,.46,.96],['CPU subtotal',31.97,43.26,55.40],['Handoff',34.39,54.61,88.77],['Tick-to-publish',74.43,99.33,119.94]];
const decision = [['Python, JSON',2667,3750,9666],['Naive Rust, JSON',1250,1750,1958],['Optimized Rust, JSON',458,625,709]];
const opacity = [.45,.72,1];
---
<Project title="QD / MADE BY AI" description="I built a Python cryptocurrency arbitrage proof of concept to verify that the opportunity was real and could be profitable, then migrated the engine to Rust and optimized latency.">
  <p slot="intro">I also built a real-time market data service in Rust. It ingests the top 20 L2 order-book levels (the API limit) from two exchanges across 11 pairs, publishes to ZeroMQ, and persists data in TimescaleDB.</p>
  <section aria-label="Market data architecture"><ol class="flow"><li><strong>2 exchanges</strong><small>11 pairs · L2 top 20</small></li><li><strong>Rust market data</strong><small>Decode · normalize · publish</small></li><li><strong>ZeroMQ Pub/Sub</strong><small>Arbitrage engine</small></li></ol><p class="note">Rust market data → TimescaleDB persistence</p></section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>Market data / tick-to-publish</h2><p class="note">Frame bytes to subscriber receipt. Excludes WebSocket read and TLS decryption.</p><div class="two-col"><figure><h3>End-to-end latency · µs</h3><div class="bar-rows">{[74.43,99.33,119.94].map((v,i)=><div class="bar-row"><span>{['p50','p99','p99.9'][i]}</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style={`width:${v/125*100}%;opacity:${opacity[i]}`}></div></div><output>{v}</output></div>)}</div><figcaption>Linear scale, 0-125 µs.</figcaption></figure><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr>{['Stage · µs','p50','p99','p99.9'].map(h=><th scope="col">{h}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{stages.map(row=><tr class:list={{subtotal:row[0]==='CPU subtotal',total:row[0]==='Tick-to-publish'}}>{row.map(v=><td>{typeof v==='number'?v.toFixed(2):v}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>Arbitrage engine / tick-to-decision</h2><p>Depth 5 optimization: p99.9 fell from 3,000 ns to 792 ns (-74%); allocations fell from 36 to 0.</p><h3>Python and Rust comparison</h3><p class="note">ZeroMQ message bytes in, arbitrage verdict out. Pre-socket only; excludes network and exchange time. Depth 5; 500,000 iterations after 50,000 warmup.</p><div class="legend">{decision.map((r,i)=><span style={`--series:var(--signal);--series-opacity:${opacity[i]}`}>{r[0]}</span>)}</div>
    <figure><svg class="chart decision-chart" viewBox="0 0 900 255" role="img" aria-label="Decision latency in nanoseconds: Python versus naive and optimized Rust at p50, p99 and p99.9">
      {[0,2500,5000,7500,10000].map(v=><g><line class="grid" x1="60" x2="875" y1={205-v/10000*185} y2={205-v/10000*185}/><text x="50" y={209-v/10000*185} text-anchor="end">{v.toLocaleString('en-US')}</text></g>)}
      {[1,2,3].map((p)=><g>{decision.map((row,i)=>{const value=Number(row[p]);const x=105+(p-1)*270+i*62;return <g><rect x={x} y={205-value/10000*185} width="44" height={value/10000*185} fill="var(--signal)" opacity={opacity[i]} rx="2"/><text x={x+22} y={197-value/10000*185} text-anchor="middle">{value.toLocaleString('en-US')}</text></g>})}<text x={189+(p-1)*270} y="233" text-anchor="middle">{['p50','p99','p99.9'][p-1]}</text></g>)}
    </svg><figcaption>Nanoseconds; linear scale. Exact values below.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr>{['Implementation · ns','p50','p99','p99.9'].map(h=><th scope="col">{h}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{decision.map(row=><tr>{row.map(v=><td>{typeof v==='number'?v.toLocaleString('en-US'):v}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>After the internship / binary wire experiment</h2><p class="compact-copy">JSON deserialization is 99.6% of the decision path; arithmetic takes 7 ns. I own the ZeroMQ publisher, so I replaced JSON with a 48-byte fixed frame.</p><dl class="metrics"><div><dt>p50</dt><dd>2 ns</dd></div><div><dt>p99</dt><dd>3 ns</dd></div><div><dt>p99.9</dt><dd>5 ns</dd></div></dl><p class="note">Measured after the internship. Excluded from the internship benchmark results above.</p></section>
</Project>
